        "id": "retained-multi-gemm-leading-dimension-gap",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The unchanged multi-GEMM wrapper does not ensure that the input and output matrix groups agree with the kernel's traversal.",
        "trigger": "An otherwise valid multi-GEMM binding call has two input matrices, one output matrix, and an indices tensor of shape (1,1).",
        "expected_behavior": "Reject incompatible group sizes before dispatch.",
        "actual_behavior": "The indices-width check agrees with the single output matrix, but the kernel iterates over the maximum of the input and output group sizes and attempts to use a second index. The inspected fused K/V and expert callers use broadcast or paired group sizes, so this example concerns the binding rather than those normal call shapes.",
